  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Mount Villard</strong> rises to 12,254 feet in Montana.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>The reliable snow-free window is roughly July through September. At this elevation, afternoon thunderstorms are a serious summer hazard \u2014 start early and plan to be off the upper mountain by midday. Outside that window expect snow travel and bring traction and navigation skills to match.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Glacier Peak, Mystic Mountain and Granite Peak (Northwest Peak) \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
